#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:3
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:5
msgid ""
"Contributions are welcome, and they are greatly appreciated! Every little "
"bit helps, and credit will always be given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:9
msgid "Types of Contributions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:11
msgid "You can contribute in many ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:14
msgid "Report Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:16
msgid "Report bugs at https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-build/issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:18
msgid "If you are reporting a bug, please include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:20
msgid "Your operating system name and version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:21
msgid ""
"Any details about your local setup that might be helpful in troubleshooting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:22
msgid "Detailed steps to reproduce the bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:25
msgid "Fix Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:27
msgid ""
"Look through the GitHub issues for bugs. Anything tagged with \"bug\" is "
"open to whoever wants to implement it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:31
msgid "Implement Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:33
msgid ""
"Look through the GitHub issues for features. Anything tagged with "
"\"feature\" is open to whoever wants to implement it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:37
msgid "Write Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:39
msgid ""
"The scikit-build project could always use more documentation. We welcome "
"help with the official scikit-build docs, in docstrings, or even on blog "
"posts and articles for the web."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:44
msgid "Submit Feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:46
msgid ""
"The best way to send feedback is to file an issue at https://github.com/"
"scikit-build/scikit-build/issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:49
msgid "If you are proposing a new feature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:51
msgid "Explain in detail how it would work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:52
msgid "Keep the scope as narrow as possible, to make it easier to implement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:53
msgid ""
"Remember that this is a volunteer-driven project, and that contributions are "
"welcome :)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:58
msgid "Get Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:60
msgid ""
"Ready to contribute? Here's how to set up ``scikit-build`` for local "
"development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:62
msgid "Fork the ``scikit-build`` repo on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:64
msgid "Clone your fork locally::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:66
msgid "$ git clone git@github.com:your_name_here/scikit-build.git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:68
msgid ""
"You can use the ``gh`` command line application to do these last two steps, "
"as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:71
msgid ""
"Make sure you have ``nox`` installed using ``pipx install nox``. If you "
"don't have pipx, you can install it with ``pip install pipx``. (You can "
"install ``nox`` with ``pip`` instead, but nox is an application, not a "
"library, and applications should always use pipx.) You can install both of "
"these packages from brew on macOS/linux. You can also use ``pipx run nox`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:78
msgid "Create a branch for local development::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:80
msgid "$ git checkout -b name-of-your-bugfix-or-feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:82
msgid "Now you can make your changes locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:84
msgid ""
"When you're done making changes, check that your changes pass our linters "
"and the tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:87
msgid "$ nox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:89
msgid ""
"If you would like to check all Python versions and you don't happen to have "
"them all installed locally, you can use the manylinux docker image instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:92
msgid ""
"$ docker run --rm -itv $PWD:/src -w /src quay.io/pypa/manylinux_2_28_x86_64:"
"latest pipx run nox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:94
msgid "Commit your changes and push your branch to GitHub::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:96
msgid ""
"$ git add -u .\n"
"$ git commit -m \"Your detailed description of your changes.\"\n"
"$ git push origin name-of-your-bugfix-or-feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:100
msgid ""
"Submit a pull request through the GitHub website or the ``gh`` command line "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:104
msgid "Pull Request Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:106
msgid "Before you submit a pull request, check that it meets these guidelines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:108
msgid "The pull request should include tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:110
msgid "If the pull request adds functionality, the docs should be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:112
msgid ""
"The pull request should work for Python 3.10+ and PyPy.  Make sure that the "
"tests pass for all supported Python versions in CI on your PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:117
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:119
msgid "To run a subset of tests::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:121
msgid "$ nox -s tests -- tests/test_skbuild.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:123
msgid "You can build and serve the docs::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:125
msgid "$ nox -s docs -- --serve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:127
msgid "You can build an SDist and a wheel in the ``dist`` folder::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CONTRIBUTING.rst:129
msgid "$ nox -s build"
msgstr ""
